drm: h713-afbd: the plane's destination rectangle is the firmware's window

Words 31..34 of the VidDec descriptor are the window the firmware fits the
picture into. This driver has always written the panel there, so the picture
has always filled the panel. They are the other half of the pair 0120 named:
words 27..30 are the window manager's m_src_cfg and stay the panel, words
31..34 are its m_dst_cfg, {h_start, h_size, v_start, v_size} in 1/16 pixel,
and it is the second one that decides where the picture lands.

The vendor's own hardware composer does exactly this for a video layer:
VideoInfo::setDisplayFrame writes the layer's rectangle into those four words
and nothing is torn down for the change (AP3c section 4.2 and 5, AP3e sections
2.2 and 2.5). Its second route, the co-processor call THal_Vp_Wce_SetWindow
(AP3 section 2.2), carries the same numbers through three physically addressed
shared buffers and a new RPC. We take the descriptor: it is already published
on every geometry change, the words are already read, and the RPC stays as the
fallback for a board that turns out not to re-run its window manager on a
republished record.

So the window is the plane's ordinary destination rectangle - CRTC_X, CRTC_Y,
CRTC_W, CRTC_H - and not a private property. Every atomic client sets it
already, and a private property would only be a second name for the same four
numbers. What changes in the check is that the plane may now be positioned and
need not cover its CRTC, and that a destination smaller than the source is
allowed: nothing in the AFBD scales, the firmware's window chain does, and
these four words are how it is told to. The bound is the smallest window this
driver will publish, one AFBD block on each axis, so the helper's scale (source
over destination) is capped at 128:1 where a 1920-wide source in a 16-wide
window is 120:1. A rectangle that would have to be clipped is refused rather
than silently shrunk.

Nothing moves until somebody asks. A plane that covers its CRTC - which is what
the check demanded until now, and what h713-tv sends - produces the identical
36-word record: h_start and v_start are zero from the memset and h_size and
v_size are the panel, word for word what 0120 wrote. Proven on the host by
compiling h713_afbd_build_video_info() out of the tree before and after this
patch and comparing all 36 words over 1920x1080, 1280x720 and 1366x768 panels
with ring and non-ring inputs: identical for the full window, and different in
exactly words 31..34 for a smaller one.

On a 1920x1080 panel our 1/16-pixel reading and the vendor's fixed 30720x17280
space are the same number (30720 * x / 1920 == x * 16). On a panel of another
size they are not, and the 1/16-pixel reading is the one measured through our
own record (0120: publishing w = 1280 put 20480 in m_src_cfg).

Not measured on a device: whether a changed m_dst_cfg alone makes the firmware
re-run its window manager (AP3c open question 7.4). If it does not, the aspect
word 35 changes with it on the path h713-tv uses - it takes the plane down and
up - and word 35 alone is known to count as a new frame (0133). The first run
belongs on a bench: a window the firmware does not like is the one thing here
that can need a power cycle.

Follow-up to 0133 (same file, the other descriptor word a client can steer);
needs nothing else. The device tree is unchanged - CRTC_X/Y/W/H are standard
properties and need no node.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

